{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Performing CRUD Operations "}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about databases."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "\"Uses the four basic functions in persistent storage to create the system.   Talks about the four basic functions for persistent storage. \""}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level. Recognizes simple ideas on persisting storage, web applications, and the functional phase of an IT project."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Continuous for Future"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We can express ideas with the<span class=\"strong\"> present continuous </span>  to talk about the future."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do you know what we are doing tomorrow in Mr. Ferguson class? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I think tomorrow we are having one of those pop quizzes he likes doing after every single topic."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The <span class=\"strong\">Present continuous</span> is commonly used to talk about situations that are happening at the moment of talking (ongoing actions), but you can also use it to express ideas in a fixed or arranged future. <br/> <br/> When a future idea is fixed or people expect it to happen since it was previously arranged such idea can be expressed using <span class=\"strong\">present continuous</span>. <br/> <br/>  If you want to make a sentence expressing future with the <span class=\"strong\">present continuous</span>, simply use the structure for such tense with a time expression showing future arrangement. <span class=\"strong\"> \u201cSubject + to be + verb + ing + complement.\u201d </span> <br/> <br/>   Example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">We are coding all those apps tomorrow morning. </span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "What is an injection attack?"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "An <span class=\"strong\">SQL injection attack</span> is an attack done by hackers to delete, steal or retrieve information from databases."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">SQL injection attacks</span> usually take place when programmers build the SQL statements dynamically by joining or concatenating the strings instead of using stored procedures. <br/> <br/>  When you use a poor design, it can allow a hacker to type some basic SQL codes into a text box in a user log in or a search box of a webpage and retrieve all the users or data information. In order to prevent such SQL injection attacks,  the programmer can use stored procedures where the prefixes differ from other prefixes used in the other user procedures."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pop quiz "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an unexpected quiz"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I think tomorrow we are having one of those pop quizzes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "catch up on "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to get or give the latest news about something to someone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It seems I'd better catch up on my studies."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "MySQL"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "open source relational database management system"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: What's all that MySQL thing about?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob04aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "query"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "instructions to elicit information from a database"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: if you know what queries to type in, everything will go really smooth"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob04aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "primary key "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "unique identification for a record in a database"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You have to use the UPDATE statement based on a the primary key you've previously created."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob04aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "chill out "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to relax"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Chill out, that's nothing you can't handle."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob04aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Read about the importance of use CRUD stead of other statements."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a brochure explaining the importance of CRUD over other programs, describe its functions and key points."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain the brochure to your classmates remarking the most important aspects about CRUD."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read about CRUD "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I recognize the importance of CRUD over other statements"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a brochure about CRUD "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain my brochure to my class"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n5le01ob04re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n5le01ob04re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">John: </span> Hi, Sharon. Do you know what we are doing tomorrow in Mr. Ferguson class? <br/><span class=\"strong\">Sharon: </span> Hmmm, let me see, taking into account last class we checked what CRUD was and the creation of databases using MySQL and its relation with CRUD statements. I think tomorrow we are having one of those pop quizzes he likes doing after every single topic. <br/><span class=\"strong\">John: </span>Wow, I missed a lot; it seems I'd better catch up on my studies. <br/>"}, {"time": "26000", "image": "enpe8n5le01ob04re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sharon: </span> If you want, I can help you out with that. <br/><span class=\"strong\">John: </span>Sure, what's all that MySQL thing about? <br/><span class=\"strong\">Sharon: </span>Well, according to Mr. Ferguson, you might want to use it to create the databases with SQL language, as all databases work with it. <br/><span class=\"strong\">John: </span> Interesting, but do you know how to create a database? <br/><span class=\"strong\">Sharon: </span>Sure, it is very simple to process, in fact if you know what queries to type in, everything will go really smooth; for example, when you are creating a new record, you have to use the INSERT statement to create such data in the database, as well as when you are updating an existing one, you have to use the UPDATE statement based on the primary key you've previously created. <br/>"}, {"time": "70000", "image": "enpe8n5le01ob04re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">John: </span>God, that's too much information to process. <br/><span class=\"strong\">Sharon: </span>Chill out, that's nothing you can't handle. <br/><span class=\"strong\">John: </span>Now, why are we using CRUD instead of any other statement? <br/><span class=\"strong\">Sharon: </span> If I'm not wrong, it is because you can use it with something called stored procedures, which is something that will protect the database from SQL injection attacks that can delete the whole database and jeopardize the performance. <br/><span class=\"strong\">John: </span>Well, that's something I ought to study before the exam."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n5le01ob04re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can tell why using CRUD is better than using other statements.  "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can explain how to create a new record using CRUD."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about how to update a record."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Why do you think safety is important at the moment of programming?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Why do you think a person would hack a database?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Is that a virus?"}], "quest